# Docker reads this, not .gitignore. One per site, because each site's build
# context is its own directory rather than the repo root. Without it the
# frontend stage copies node_modules from the host into the build, which is slow
# and pointless since the image installs its own from the lockfile.
**/node_modules
**/build
**/bin
# Compiled inside the build stage; shipping the host's copy in would only
# slow the context transfer.
**/og
# Runtime state. The log database is the fastest-growing file in this repo and
# sending it in the build context would dominate every single build.
**/data
.git
.playwright-cli
**/.env
**/*.pem
